+## 6. Maintenance protocol
+
+- **Dep bump:** edit `requirements-dev.txt` → `uv pip compile requirements-dev.txt -o requirements-dev.lock` → commit both (lock body = the reviewable resolution diff).
+- **uv bump:** bump the `version:` input in all 3 setup-uv steps **and** recompile the lock in the same commit (resolver-version coupling).
+- **pyyaml bump:** one-line `pyyaml==` change at the 3 install sites, single commit.
+- **Freshness-gate triage:** a red gate = lock no longer matches manifest — recompile; never hand-edit the lock.
+
+## 7. Alternatives rejected
+
+1. **setup-uv without `version:` pin** — freshness determinism drifts with uv releases. 2. **`pip install uv` bootstrap** — reintroduces the pip chain into the <10s preflight job. 3. **Second lock for pyyaml** — one-package surface; inline pin suffices. 4. **Domain locks now** — deferred WITH census evidence: no CI job installs domain requirements today; unconsumed locks are speculative surface. 5. **`uv sync` / pyproject rewrite** — rejected by the WO itself (requirements.txt stays SSOT). 6. **`uv.lock` binary** — text locks are diff-reviewable, `pip install -r` fallback preserved.
